                    {
                        "sense_id": "3c15a3ad-c5cf-3146-b651-e3acb901a725",
                        "entry_id": "1bc2db68-fb36-39b4-91d4-28be4a840c5b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The capital city of Malacca State, Malaysia."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "412a64d5-fb3d-30f0-b053-f7bf2f3b773a",
                        "entry_id": "1bc2db68-fb36-39b4-91d4-28be4a840c5b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ellipsis of Strait of Malacca."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "ellipsis"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "21bf0fd8-896d-4c25-a272-a57e1f9376ef",
                                "sense_id": "412a64d5-fb3d-30f0-b053-f7bf2f3b773a",
                                "text": "The Arabs were not pioneers on this route; even earlier than this period Indian ships had sailed through Malacca to Java and went as far as China."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92472e25-3491-487e-a432-8a2885e76c48",
                                "sense_id": "412a64d5-fb3d-30f0-b053-f7bf2f3b773a",
                                "text": "Consider these facts : • In just one year, U.S. $ 400 billion in cargo — including 80 percent of the oil transported to Northeast Asia moves through Malacca on 60,000 ships; • Of the 15 largest ports in the world, 12 are in the Asia […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "11cf662c-5c9d-4d72-b4c2-768434fda9cd",
                                "sense_id": "412a64d5-fb3d-30f0-b053-f7bf2f3b773a",
                                "text": "Moreover, the per barrel cost of pumping oil through Burma to Yunnan and then refining it and transporting it to market will likely be several times the cost of carrying it through Malacca on a supertanker to Eastern China's large demand centers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "892979c0-9d86-4a59-b067-5bc66a93480c",
                                "sense_id": "412a64d5-fb3d-30f0-b053-f7bf2f3b773a",
                                "text": "[…] when the Portuguese had owned a de facto monopoly on shipping routes across the Indian Ocean, through Malacca to the Indies, and along the Pacific coast […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c318f201-5a66-4d54-adc7-ba7b266e96e5",
                        "source_entry_id": "1bc2db68-fb36-39b4-91d4-28be4a840c5b",
                        "source_sense_description": "state in Malaysia",
                        "target_lang_word": "Malacca",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Malacca",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7cea50a-5ba1-3922-8e1d-4ee9ac5b7eae",
                                        "entry_id": "d1635452-da44-376c-aa7a-b041301a4e95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ville et État de Malaisie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b14e409e-0a3e-4391-9935-930f1648a80e",
                                                "sense_id": "a7cea50a-5ba1-3922-8e1d-4ee9ac5b7eae",
                                                "text": "Mr. Beauvisage a fait l’analyse d’une plante trouvée par Mr. Brau de Saint Pol Lias dans la presqu’île de Malacca et envoyée par lui au Muséum de Paris."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1b9eadd-43f1-4b71-968d-ff5cba54d6e0",
                                                "sense_id": "a7cea50a-5ba1-3922-8e1d-4ee9ac5b7eae",
                                                "text": "Il manque également une babiole à laquelle je suis attaché, une canne en jonc de Malacca avec mon chiffre gravé sur la virole."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "764337ec-d849-36e0-8029-66b249a306ca",
                                        "entry_id": "d1635452-da44-376c-aa7a-b041301a4e95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Détroit entre l’Indonésie (Sumatra) et la côte Ouest de la péninsule malaise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19b0f49c-8640-4d90-854c-9307a0ac63ee",
                                                "sense_id": "764337ec-d849-36e0-8029-66b249a306ca",
                                                "text": "Ils franchirent l’océan Indien, remontant sans fin vers le nord-est, firent une halte sur l’île de Ceylan, avant d’enfiler le détroit de Malacca et croiser au large de Singapour, puis ils gagnèrent le golfe de Siam avant, d’enfin, atteindre l’île d’Hainan dans le golfe du Tonkin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
